**Where inputs contradicted each other and how I resolved it**

- Held reads: my earlier text said the owner had agreed to include them. That was wrong. The document states the mob consensus wording (optional, additive, off by default, never a condition of meeting reachability) as the recommendation and lists it as open.
- The inbox candidate shape: my revision carried only the announcement descriptor; the merged edit list requires both meeting descriptors and both inbox descriptors. The document carries all four and bounds nested resolution to one level.
- The original design's relay and rendezvous frames and steps conflicted with the P2P invariant; the document has neither. The frame set is eight frames with no reachability control, and both conventions are marked as conventions.
- Punching: the original design said "attach a UDP channel to the reflexive address", which would bind a new socket. The document adopts the same-socket rule and the nonce-bearing pong as the confirmation.
- Dedup for `:meet/here`: my revision relied on re-reading announcements; the document requires stable request ids with M-side deduplication and one active pair per peer id, keeping the re-read as recovery guidance only.
